Search's failure reaches users through the frontend's `/hotels` endpoint, and nothing else in the abnormal period fails, so I'm stopping here.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'search%' AND metric IN ('k8s.container.ready','k8s.container.restarts') ORDER BY time", "claim": "Search pod container stays not ready (0) while its restart count climbs from 2 to 5+ during the incident."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'abn' p, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', count(*) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='search'", "claim": "Search emits no spans in the abnormal window, though it produced many in the normal window."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('HTTP /hotels','search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Every frontend search.Search/Nearby client call errors, and every HTTP /hotels request returns 500."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels') OR (service_name='frontend' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Search outage turns frontend's /hotels user requests into 500 errors via failed search calls."}]}
  ]
}
```

